; The errors beancount's grammar raises as it reads a posting are reported
; when a later syntax error drops the transaction: a cost spec's once its
; braces close, a posting's once its line ends.
2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-01 open Assets:Cash

2020-01-05 * "negative total price, then a syntax error"
  Assets:A      4 HOOL @@ -10 USD
  Assets:Cash   10 USD #tag

2020-01-06 * "merge cost, then a syntax error"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL {*, 100 USD, *}
  Assets:Cash ^link

2020-01-07 * "merge cost, a syntax error on its line"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL {*} #tag
  Assets:Cash

2020-01-08 * "negative price, a syntax error on its line"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL @ -2 USD #tag
  Assets:Cash

2020-01-09 * "price in another currency than the cost, then a syntax error"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL {2 EUR} @ 3 USD
  Assets:Cash  -2 EUR EUR

2020-01-10 * "compound inside total braces, then an invalid token"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL {{2 # 3 EUR}}
  Assets:Cash  -2 EUR
bad

2020-01-11 * "total price without units, then a syntax error"
  Assets:A  HOOL @@ 5 USD
  Assets:Cash  -2 EUR EUR
